## Client configuration

### Environment variables

```
REDIS_CLUSTER_ENABLED=true
REDIS_CLUSTER_NODES={{ ci_seeds | join(',') }}
REDIS_USERNAME=
REDIS_PASSWORD={{ '<ask DevOps>' if ci_auth else '' }}
REDIS_TLS={{ 'true' if ci_tls else 'false' }}
```

Keep username, password and TLS as settings even when empty, so production only changes values, not code.

### Spring Boot 3 (Lettuce), `application-dev.yml`

```yaml
spring:
  data:
    redis:
      cluster:
        nodes: {{ ci_seeds | join(',') }}
        max-redirects: 3
      timeout: 2s
{% if ci_auth %}
      password: ${REDIS_PASSWORD}
{% endif %}
{% if ci_tls %}
      ssl:
        enabled: true
{% endif %}
      lettuce:
        cluster:
          refresh:
            adaptive: true   # follow failovers quickly
            period: 30s
```

### Java, Lettuce

```java
List<RedisURI> seeds = Stream.of({{ hosts | map('regex_replace', '^(.*)$', '"\\1"') | join(', ') }})
    .map(h -> RedisURI.create(h, {{ redis_port }})).toList();

RedisClusterClient client = RedisClusterClient.create(seeds);
client.setOptions(ClusterClientOptions.builder()
    .topologyRefreshOptions(ClusterTopologyRefreshOptions.builder()
        .enableAllAdaptiveRefreshTriggers()
        .enablePeriodicRefresh(Duration.ofSeconds(30))
        .build())
    .build());
StatefulRedisClusterConnection<String, String> conn = client.connect();
```

