## Things to know when coding against it

- **The client must reach all nodes on {{ redis_port }}.** Clients get redirected (`MOVED`/`ASK`) to whichever node owns a key's slot.
- **Multi-key commands need a shared hash tag.** `MGET`, `MSET`, transactions and Lua scripts only work when all keys are in one slot: `{user:42}:profile`, `{user:42}:cart`. Otherwise you get `CROSSSLOT`.
- **Memory is small{{ ' and nothing is evicted' if ci_policy == 'noeviction' else '' }}.** {{ ci_maxmem | int | human_readable }} per master{{ ', so writes fail with `OOM` when a shard is full. Set TTLs on cache keys.' if ci_policy == 'noeviction' else '.' }}
- **Plan for a few seconds of failover.** Node timeout is {{ redis_cluster_node_timeout // 1000 }} s. Enable topology refresh and retry on connection errors.
- **DEV may be rebuilt or wiped at any time.** Don't store anything you need to keep.
